# Expo Router screens and layouts

- Route files stay thin: layout, wiring, and navigation. Data access, calculations, and side effects live in hooks, services, or repositories under `src/`.
- App-wide gates (auth, license, onboarding, app lock) sit in the root `_layout.tsx`, never per tab or per screen.
- Splash: call `SplashScreen.preventAutoHideAsync()` at module scope and hide once the root is ready. A fail-safe timeout must not fire after boot succeeded and must not hide a real boot error or skip a gate that is still loading.
- Export `ErrorBoundary` from the root layout (re-export expo-router's or provide one with a retry action) so a render error never shows a white screen.
- `Link`: pass a single style object, never a style array. Use `asChild` with a `Pressable` for custom content.
- Typed routes (`experiments.typedRoutes`): build hrefs with the generated types; don't cast to `any` or `as Href` to silence errors.
- Read params with `useLocalSearchParams` and validate them (ids can be missing or non-numeric after a deep link).
- Modals and custom sheets close on Android back: `Modal onRequestClose`, or `BackHandler` in a focus effect that removes its listener.
- Screens with lists or inputs follow `react-native/components-and-lists.mdc` and `react-native/forms-and-keyboard.mdc`.
- Header buttons and menu actions read current state when pressed (refs or callbacks from a store), not values captured at first render.
